      "description": "Watch Montenegro vs Cyprus highlights and goals from UEFA Nations League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 25, 2026. A tense tactical battle in the UEFA Nations League On September 25, 2026 , Montenegro and Cyprus faced off in a highly anticipated UEFA Nations League fixture. The match began with a cagey atmosphere, as both teams prioritized defensive stability and discipline, underscored by an early yellow card for Konstantinos Soteriou just three minutes into the game. Turning the tide in the second half Following a scoreless first half, the game ignited shortly after the interval. In the 55th minute, Marcus Edwards broke the deadlock for Cyprus , converting an assist from Nicholas Tsaroulla . The setback acted as a catalyst for Montenegro , who upped their attacking pressure. Their persistence paid off in the 66th minute when Nikola Krstovic stepped up to the spot and calmly dispatched a penalty to level the score, following an earlier booking for Nicholas Tsaroulla . The decisive moment As both managers turned to their benches to inject fresh energy into the closing stages, the momentum swung firmly in favour of the hosts. With just four minutes of regular time remaining, Nikola Krstovic provided the pivotal assist of the night. Milutin Osmajic latched onto the pass and fired home the winner, sending the home crowd into raptures. Despite late pressure from the visitors, Montenegro held firm until the final whistle to secure a significant result."
